00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.290
Rhiannon: Psychotherapy, talking
therapy, counselling, or simply

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:12.609
therapy, are some of the terms used
as alternatives to medication and

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.500
can really benefit people struggling
with emotional difficulties, life

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.859
challenges, and mental health concerns.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:23.189
Medication can reduce some of the
symptoms of mental health conditions,

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.100
but therapy teaches people skills to
address symptoms on their own, and

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.980
these can stay with the individual after
therapy ends, and as symptoms improve,

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.300
the need for treatment may reduce.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:40.950
Untreated mental health issues often
get worse and may have other negative

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.320
effects affecting work, study,
relationships and general health.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.640
A therapist can give support
going forward, and once a crisis

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.960
is over, they can be a safe
haven for when things get tough.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:01.665
Psychological therapies services are
also known as Improving Access to

00:01:01.666 --> 00:01:05.076
Psychological Therapies [IAPT] services.

00:01:05.676 --> 00:01:10.716
Examples of these are, talking therapies
like counselling for depression, and

00:01:10.756 --> 00:01:15.666
cognitive behavioural therapy [CBT]
and are available on the NHS with

00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:18.106
referral from a GP or self-referral.

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:23.256
There are many different types of
‘talking therapy’, but they all involve

00:01:23.266 --> 00:01:25.135
working with a trained therapist.

00:01:25.736 --> 00:01:29.356
The therapist helps find answers
to the problems the child

00:01:29.376 --> 00:01:30.916
or young person is having.

00:01:32.016 --> 00:01:36.196
One type of talking therapy may be
better than another, and different

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:42.706
talking therapies suit different people.

